+# Bug Fix: Deleted products break carts and orders
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T21:50:44Z
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Cart hydration now removes only persisted lines whose catalog product no longer exists, deletes their dependent attributes, and keeps the cart available when it becomes empty. Cart serialization always emits an empty product list, and attempts to add a missing SKU use the API's 404 not-found exception; order snapshot fields remain independent of the deleted catalog row.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java` | modified | Sanitize deleted-product lines during cart reads and stop deleting empty carts. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartDataPopulator.java` | modified | Serialize empty carts with an empty item list. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Missing SKU add requests raise `ResourceNotFoundException`. |
+
+## Diff Highlights
+
+Missing cart items are removed from the refreshed line-item set and their attributes are deleted before the cart is updated. `getById` and `getByCode` now return that sanitized cart even when no lines remain, allowing totals to calculate as zero.
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- No new test source was added; existing focused cart tests were run. The repository's available integration fixtures do not cover the complete delete-product/order-history sequence.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed.
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-core -am -Dtest=ShoppingCartTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed (1 test, 0 failures).
+- Commands run: `./mvnw -pl sm-shop -am -Dtest=ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest,OrderApiIntegrationTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed (8 tests, 0 failures, 1 skipped; cart integration reported 7/7).
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The assessment proposed adding dedicated deletion/order regression tests. No new tests were added because the checkout has no existing fixture covering the required product-delete lifecycle; implementation and available cart regressions were verified instead.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add an integration fixture that creates a product, cart, and order, deletes the product, and exercises all required merchant/customer endpoints.
